sentences.l:
Nor did the old man forget his guileful device,
but first of all he became a well-maned lion,
and then a serpent, and a leopard, and a great boar;

until you come again to the water of Egypt, the sky-fallen river,
and offer sacred hecatombs
to the immortal gods, who hold the wide sky;

But him a watchman saw from a watch-post, whom indeed had set there,
leading him, Aegisthus of guileful counsel, and promised as a reward
two talents of gold;
